m.daisy.new () 
{ 
    ( if (($# < 1 || $# > 2)) || [[ ! $1 =~ ^[0-9]{4}$ ]]; then
        printf '%s\n' 'Usage: m.daisy.new ISO_YEAR [EXISTING_PARENT_DIRECTORY]' 1>&2;
        exit 2;
    fi;
    local archive_year=$1 archive_parent=. archive_dir;
    local year_number=$((10#$1)) prior january_first weeks=52 week day coordinate;
    (($# == 1)) || archive_parent=$2;
    ((year_number > 0)) || exit 2;
    prior=$((year_number - 1));
    january_first=$(((prior + prior / 4 - prior / 100 + prior / 400) % 7 + 1));
    if ((january_first == 4 || (january_first == 3 && year_number % 4 == 0 &&
                (year_number % 100 != 0 || year_number % 400 == 0)))); then
        weeks=53;
    fi;
    cd -- "$archive_parent" || exit;
    archive_dir="$PWD/daisy_$archive_year";
    mkdir -- "$archive_dir" || exit;
    sed "s/@DAISY_YEAR@/$archive_year/g" > "$archive_dir/README.md" <<'DAISY_README' || 
# Daisy @DAISY_YEAR@

Public annual archive for ISO week-year **@DAISY_YEAR@**. The directory
421/ represents full Daisy coordinate @DAISY_YEAR@/421: week 42, Monday.
The year is already in the repository name. The starter creates every
valid WWD/ directory for this ISO year; SB Shell maintains the organization
and publication sequence beyond that date structure.

The archive contains public source records and deliberate publication
copies. Keep private working documents, identity information and signing
keys outside this repository and its Git history.

## Tools that can use or write this archive

| Tool | Role and current boundary |
| --- | --- |
| [Daisy](https://github.com/johnrigler/daisy) | Independent Bash functions, saved function artifacts and date conventions. |
| [Mogwai](https://github.com/johnrigler/mogwai) | Reusable tools, this year template and optional integrations. The archive remains ordinary files after creation. |
| [SB Shell](https://github.com/johnrigler/mogwai/tree/main/sbshell) | Mogwai component: maintain and present the archive as ordered issues/pages, with local PHP assembly and static HTML publication. |
| [FileProxy](https://github.com/johnrigler/mogwai/tree/main/fileProxy) | Mogwai component: register this archive as its own root; read/write local files and generate its SQLite catalog and root files.txt inventory. Registration and scanning do not push Git commits. |
| [SB Stats](https://github.com/johnrigler/sbstats) | Collectors, journals, data and charts can be written here through an explicitly chosen output path. No adapter is installed by this starter. |
| crypto-python | User-named prospective writer; its exact repository and output interface still need to be linked. |
| [Chisel](https://github.com/johnrigler/chisel) | Optional transaction tooling and public transaction records. Keep WIFs and private keys outside the archive. |
| [CertLedger](https://github.com/johnrigler/certLedger) | Legal/administrative context and verification tools; public release follows removal of private case material. |

Choose the destination explicitly in each writer. Other tools may write
ordinary files into the same directory tree. They do not need to adopt a
new record schema or run a Mogwai service.

## Work locally

For today's coordinate, first check that the local ISO year matches:

~~~bash
test "$(date +%G)" = "@DAISY_YEAR@" && printf '%s\n' "$(date +%V%u)"
~~~

Set TZ=America/Denver when the machine uses a different archival timezone.
Daisy core's d.today produces a full YYYY/WWD path; use the WWD coordinate
directly within this year-scoped checkout.

For a default checkout at $HOME/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@, register FileProxy:

~~~bash
cd "$HOME/mogwai/fileProxy"
python3 fp.py add-root daisy@DAISY_YEAR@ "$HOME/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@"
python3 fp.py scan daisy@DAISY_YEAR@
~~~

FileProxy keeps the actual catalog.sqlite3 and generated root files.txt
in the registered archive by default. Commit an inspected, consistent
database snapshot when publishing it; SQLite WAL/SHM files are transient.
Preserve ALP's .files.txt, which has a separate meaning.

To browse this archive with Mogwai's SB Shell component:

~~~bash
bash "$HOME/mogwai/sbshell/setup" check "$HOME/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@"
cd "$HOME/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@"
php -S 127.0.0.1:39692 -t . "$HOME/mogwai/sbshell/cruff/index.php"
~~~

Use your installed PHP 8+ binary with SQLite3 and GD. Files and the actual
SQLite catalog stay in this archive; both tool implementations live in
Mogwai. Add this repository's path to your home config when it should be
included in your normal repository-pull command.

SB Shell's current static navigation uses a root files.txt with paths
relative to that root. Numbered files and symlinks provide editorial order
inside chosen units. The local PHP assembler can build the long HTML page;
publish its HTML and required assets for static hosting or IPFS. Chrome
handles printing to US Letter. GitHub Pages does not execute PHP.

## Publish the new repository

Create an empty **public** daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@ repository on GitHub, then:

~~~bash
cd "$HOME/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@"
git init -b main
git add .
git commit -m "Start Daisy @DAISY_YEAR@"
git remote add origin https://github.com/johnrigler/daisy_@DAISY_YEAR@.git
git push -u origin main
~~~

Adjust the owner and local path when using a different account/location.
The starter creates local files; remote repository creation and publication
are explicit operations.

## Closing the ISO year

An ISO year can extend into early January of the next calendar year.
ISO 2026 ends January 3, 2027; ISO 2027 begins January 4. Mogwai carries the tools that prepare and publish these files. Archiving the
closed source tree and SQLite catalog to IPFS and combined GitHub/IPFS
lookup remain planned features:
[annual archive plan](https://github.com/johnrigler/mogwai/blob/main/fileProxy/docs/ANNUAL-IPFS-ARCHIVE.md).
DAISY_README
 exit
    cat > "$archive_dir/AGENTS.md" <<'DAISY_AGENTS' || 
# Annual Daisy archive

- This archive is intended for public records. Keep private working files,
  identity information, credentials and signing keys outside its Git history.
- The year is in daisy_YYYY; dated paths beneath it are ISO WWD/.
  Preserve existing historical paths; do not insert another YYYY/.
- SB Shell maintains editorial order beyond the dated structure. Preserve
  numbered parts and intended symlink placement.
- FileProxy's root files.txt is a generated root-relative inventory.
  ALP's .files.txt is different and may contain executable loading actions.
- Publish the actual, inspected SQLite catalog when needed; do not fabricate
  catalog entries or ledger/IPFS references.
- Daisy works independently. Keep reusable tooling in its source repository.
  Saved Bash functions retain their original names and content-derived IDs.
DAISY_AGENTS
 exit
    cat > "$archive_dir/.gitignore" <<'DAISY_IGNORE' || 
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
DAISY_IGNORE
 exit
    for ((week = 1; week <= weeks; week++))
    do
        for ((day = 1; day <= 7; day++))
        do
            printf -v coordinate '%02d%d' "$week" "$day";
            mkdir -- "$archive_dir/$coordinate" || exit;
            : > "$archive_dir/$coordinate/.gitkeep" || exit;
        done;
    done;
    printf 'Created %s with %d ISO week/day directories.\n' "$archive_dir" "$((weeks * 7))" )
}
